<title>PERU: Peru's bank liquidity rises 2.8 percent in Oct.</title>
<headline>Peru's bank liquidity rises 2.8 percent in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's total banking system liquidity rose 2.8 percent to 29.895 billion soles during October, the Central Reserve Bank said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Liquidity in the local sol currency fell 1.4 percent to 9.431 billion soles in October, according to the bank's weekly report.  Foreign currency liquidity rose 2.3 percent to $7.963 billion in the same period.</p>
<p>Total liquidity stood at 22.483 billion soles at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
